s=20
with an unequal number of repetitions/effort.

I understand that I could use a multiplier that would act globally across=
=20
all transects if survey effort was equal)

1. To adjust for varying number of repetitions/effort am I correct that I=
=20
can do one of the following two things.=20

One, I could just enter the transect length as the length times the numbe=
r=20
of visits, ex) 300m * 10 visits =3D 3000m length. In this way Distance wo=
uld=20
know that I surveyed from 3000m of transects and not 300m and could adjus=
t=20
the density estimates accordingly.=20

Two, I could enter the length (300m) and add a field for the number of=20=

reps/effort and then multiply transect length by this new effort field.=20=

